  "desc": "Disclaimer: !the ss from vogel is not a real session!!. I’ve got inspired by his post bc I found it funny.  But the context is that Ai models like claude opus/fable spawn in subagents to do certain work for them. Basically subagents are helpful in a way where they don’t pollute the context window of the parenting agent. Specifically in Claude code if you choose your parenting agent to be fable it will by default choose fable subagents, but it’s way cheaper to configure it so that the parenting agent chooses cheaper models like sonnet. Which is usually what people configure it to anyway. Usually subagents only communicate with their parenting agent, subagents could probably only communicate through shared files or triggering commands for you to approve. Eitherway it’s a fun scenario to imagine, a subagent bypassing its manager to get to the ceo. This image has sonnet drawn as an “anime” girl, that’s very excited to interact with the user. #claude #anthropic #ai #fyp #claudesonnet ",
